                      </tr>
                    ))
                  }
                </tbody>
              </table>
              <div class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-5 py-3">
                <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">
                  Applies where conductors are bundled for more than 24 inches. Grounds never count; the
                  neutral counts only per 310.15(E).
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
            Sources &amp; standards: NEC (NFPA 70) 2023 — Table 310.16 ampacities, Table 310.15(B)(1) ambient
            correction, 310.15(B)(3) rooftop sunlight exposure, Table 310.15(C)(1) bundling adjustment,
            310.15(E) neutral and grounding conductor counting, 110.14(C) termination temperature limitations,
            240.4(B) and 240.4(D) overcurrent protection. Local amendments override the model code.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

